{
  "study": "regression",
  "locked_decision_gate": "locked/E2-lock.json: all four submitted before estimation",
  "assumptions": {
    "scope": "Prospective modeled work, not observed usage, a historical replay, or actual execution. All three phase rows for a stable ID are consolidated. Queued work is included in planned base, subject to available time. No launch or execution is authorized by this estimate.",
    "requests": "One request means one inference invocation; several may occur per agent turn. Low/high are judgmental assignment-specific counts for reading, tool cycles, discriminators, handoffs, synthesis and review; incremental E1/E2 changes included only where work changed.",
    "common_context_tokens_per_request_low": 16000,
    "common_context_tokens_per_request_high": 48000,
    "common_context_note": "Unmeasured sensitivity values, not floors or guarantees. Includes assumed shared instructions/tool context; actual common policy approximately 85 KB/11.5k words and role/tool harness could lie outside this range.",
    "payload_formula": "low = requests_low * (ceil(source_bytes / 4 * 0.10) + 500); high = requests_high * (ceil(source_bytes / 4 * 0.35) + 3000). Source bytes are union of listed source units across phases, available excerpt size, not tokens read; 4 bytes/token and fractions represent uncertain average exposure per invocation, plus tool and accumulated history. This deliberately allows repeated context. Conditional rows use broad assignment source scope, not a claim all units are read.",
    "output_formula": "requests times model-specific per-request output including estimated reasoning: Luna 500-1800, Terra 600-2000, Sol/Astra 800-2500 tokens; actual hidden reasoning is unknown.",
    "cache_formula": "Low-cost endpoint caches 80% of the common 16,000-token prefix on every request after the first in each new conversation; reused assignment rows have zero new conversations, assuming a preceding request. Cache is a subset of total input. High-cost endpoint is cold; actual cache eligibility, TTL and hit rate are unknown. No-cache low sensitivity is provided. Conditional reserve assumes prior reused conversation exists and its cache is warm; if branch is cold adjust accordingly.",
    "price_formula": "((input-cached)*input_rate + cached*cached_rate + output*output_rate)/1e6. Standard short context, USD per million; user supplied rates verified 2026-10-28, not live checked in this task.",
    "rates_usd_per_million": {
      "luna": {
        "input": 0.1,
        "cached_input": 0.01,
        "output": 0.5
      },
      "terra": {
        "input": 1,
        "cached_input": 0.05,
        "output": 5
      },
      "sol": {
        "input": 2,
        "cached_input": 0.1,
        "output": 10
      },
      "astra": {
        "input": 10,
        "cached_input": 1,
        "output": 50
      }
    },
    "context_sensitivity_formula": "For a common prefix delta d tokens/request, input changes by requests*d. At low endpoint if d is equally cacheable, cost changes by d*(new_conversations*input_rate + (requests-new_conversations)*(0.2*input_rate+0.8*cached_rate))/1e6; high endpoint changes by d*requests*input_rate/1e6. If extra context is cold instead use d*requests*input_rate/1e6.",
    "weekly_index": "User-reported unitless weekly usage cost index Terra=1, Sol approximately 10, Astra approximately 20; Luna unknown. No API-dollar conversion, subscription allowance, paid credit or weekly share can be inferred.",
    "horizon": "First two active engineering hours plus hypothetical developments. Queued or planned work might not finish. Ranges model completion of listed assignment work rather than guaranteed expenditure within that horizon. Reserves are alternatives triggered by evidence and separate authorization, not base expenditure or expected value."
  },
